        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ecb3fffe-3bb2-5fe2-8471-ac6f5285ce1a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Belarusian State Technological University\n- Places: Minsk, Belarus, Gomel, Sverdlovsk, Yekaterinburg, Sverdlovsk Oblast, Russia\n- People: Yakov Sverdlov\n- Topics: engineering and technology, city renaming\n\nFacts:\n- In 1924, Yekaterinburg was renamed Sverdlovsk after Communist party leader Yakov Sverdlov.\n- In 1930, Belarusian State Technological University was established in Gomel as the Forestry Institute.\n- In 1941, Belarusian State Technological University was evacuated to Sverdlovsk, now called Yekaterinburg.\n- In 1991, Sverdlovsk was renamed back to Yekaterinburg.\n- As of 2010, Yekaterinburg had a population of 1,349,772 and was Russia's fourth-largest city after Moscow, Saint Petersburg, and Novosibirsk.\n- Yekaterinburg is the administrative centre of Sverdlovsk Oblast and lies in the middle of the Eurasian continent on the border of Europe and Asia.\n- Belarusian State Technological University is a university in Minsk, Belarus that specializes in engineering and technology.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
